# The direct dependencies of a contributor's checkout, by name: the runtime set plus what the
# tests and the linter need. Versions live in `requirements-dev.txt`, for the reason its
# runtime counterpart gives.
#
# `requirements-dev.txt`, before it became a lock, carried `pytest>=9.1.1,<10`,
# `httpx2>=2.13.1,<3` and `ruff==0.16.9`. None of those bounds is restated here, and that is a
# decision rather than an oversight: a range here is the second place a version is decided that
# the lock exists to remove. Both halves went, not just the caps. The floors and ruff's exact
# pin are now facts of the lock, which sits on all three today; the caps are simply gone, so
# nothing stops the next regeneration taking `httpx2` 3.x, `pytest` 10.x or a ruff minor with
# new default rules. What catches that is the suite and the linter running against the
# regenerated lock, in the same change that regenerates it -- and for the `>=2.13.1` floor,
# which Dependabot raised in #99 and is the one bound here with a recorded reason, that the
# lock is only ever moved forward. A bound that genuinely has to hold belongs in a constraints
# file passed to the compile command, so that it is still one decision and not two.

-r requirements.in

httpx2
pytest
ruff

# Imported directly by `tests/test_compose_topology.py` and `tests/test_dependency_lock.py`,
# so it is asked for here rather than relied on as a transitive of `uvicorn[standard]`: an
# extra that stopped pulling it in would take two test modules with it, which is the shape of
# a version decided nowhere.
pyyaml
